# The skip between acts (scripts/acts.gd; Alex, 2026-11-24: "the time skip is the player's choice").
# Each act's last goal sets act_ready; her bed's "Begin the next chapter…" or the Esc menu's row then
# plays act<N>_begin, never on its own. The first choice is the confirm: "Not yet" changes nothing.
# @act next makes the skip (the act, her age and model, the calendar, act_ready cleared, the next
# act's goals; going into Act 2, Gran's passing and the end of her rent), @act card shows the
# montage card of what she has. The format is at the top of scripts/story.gd.
# Every line here is a DRAFT for Alex.

== act2_begin
@requires act_ready
? Begin the next chapter? Twenty-five years will pass, and everything you own comes with you.
- Begin it. -> go
- Not yet.
@end
@label go
@fade out 1.5
@act next
@title Twenty-five years later
@act card
@fade in 1.5
Nora (warm): Fifty. Somewhere along the way the farm stopped being Gran's and started being mine.
> The needles are the same pair. Her hands know them better now.

